  "notes": "Agent re-read after the Code Health refactor, 2026-11-07, under the owner directive transcribed in verification/reviews/rulings/agent-rereview-after-refactor-2026-11-07.md. This record is NOT an owner signature: it attests the agent's substantive reading only. Read proxy.continuation_installation: app.rs became app.rs plus app/{boot,planes,transport,capabilities,serving}.rs. The continuation wiring moved verbatim into app/capabilities.rs::with_correlation: mrtr_continuation_store(&continuation_plan(), control)?.into_parts(), the store attached only when Some with DEFAULT_CONTINUATION_TTL_SECS, and Seam::MrtrContinuationStore declared exactly once from the same value. continuation_installation_test now reads the whole composition tree (composition_production()) and its three counts (one with_continuation_store, one mrtr_continuation_store, one Seam::MrtrContinuationStore) hold on the new tree; the two cited rule tests differ from the old only in message text and in that reader. serving_capabilities/continuation.rs, config_state/continuation_control.rs, startup_posture.rs and seam.rs have no diff. The claim holds. Every cited Rust test still exists by name; I compared each one's body with its body at the last record's commit and name the ones that differ. Helper functions that unchanged test bodies call were not all diffed. The mutation lane was not run. Evidence class as registered.",
